# Bot1 names Brazen Borrower. A spell on the stack as an Adventure has only the Adventure's characteristics (CR 715.4),
# its name Petty Theft, so Bot2's Petty Theft is not a "spell with the chosen name" and costs its printed {1}{U}.
# Bot2 floats {U}{U}{B}{R}, more than the Adventure would cost if it were taxed; only two mana is spent and two remain
# (a Brazen Borrower cast as the creature would owe {2} more). Bot2 holds the surplus because the engine's advice for
# whether an Adventure is affordable still judges its cost against the card in hand (`least_cost` in actions.rs), so
# with exactly {1}{U} Petty Theft is not offered; the cast itself, shown here, is right.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Anointed Peacekeeper
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Brazen Borrower
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Anointed Peacekeeper.Cast
Bot1.Name(Brazen Borrower)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
? Bot2.Mana = {U}{U}{B}{R}
Bot2.Hand.Brazen Borrower.Cast(Sol Ring; Ability: Adventure; Spend: U, U)
? Stack = Petty Theft
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Mana = {B}{R}
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Exile = Brazen Borrower
